{"results":[{"url":"https://www.facebook.com/ameer.lukmanharuna/posts/the-igbos-on-average-are-richer-than-any-ethnic-group-in-nigeria-some-accounts-s/1787600978102597/","final_url":"https://www.facebook.com/ameer.lukmanharuna/posts/the-igbos-on-average-are-richer-than-any-ethnic-group-in-nigeria-some-accounts-s/1787600978102597/","title":"Ameer Lukman Haruna","description":"The Igbos, on average, are richer than any ethnic group in Nigeria, some accounts say Africa. And this is true whether in Lagos, Abuja, Maiduguri or Portharcourt. The Igbos in Nigeria share the same...","language":"en","text":"## Ameer Lukman Haruna's Post\n\n---\n\n### **Ameer Lukman Haruna**\n\nFebruary 2, 2022\n\nThe Igbos, on average, are richer than any ethnic group in Nigeria, some accounts say Africa. And this is true whether in Lagos, Abuja, Maiduguri or Portharcourt. The Igbos in Nigeria share the same weather conditions with everybody. They are subjected to the same government policies. They are not genetically different from everyone. The question is: What makes the Igbos successful and generally more prosperous than anyone? The simple answer is: Culture. The culture of entrepreneurship, the culture that encourages individual initiative, the culture that does not confer unnecessary reverence to hierarchy. The culture that attaches a premium price to education. The culture that says womenfolk matters. Igbos are also frugal, disciplined, resilient, tenacious, and above all, comfortable anywhere.\n\nAll reactions:\n\n11 comments\n\n7 shares\n\nLike\n\nComment\n\nMost relevant\n\n\n\nOkenwa Harrison\n\nThen allow Igbos rule Nigeria and see how Nigeria will become prosperous in just a few years.\n\n* 4y\n\nView all 6 replies\n\nNura Aliyu\n\nYeah that's true IGBO are very resilience and hard-working people , they are really\n\ngood in business and making alot of things that can make them to stand up with their own two feet. The ideas behind the Igbo people success in business is that they make a good and huge sacrifices and patience all the times\n\n* 4y\n\nKabiru Ahmad Mahmud\n\nThey can do everything possible good or bad to get rich.\n\n* 4y\n\n1\n\nComr Ibrahim Babaji\n\nThank you for this great piece. The igbos uses their chances unlike us in arewa. We lack the culture of empowering our families and friends. When you rise alone, you shall not have a support on your way down. Let's adopt the culture of empowerment.\n\n* 4y\n\nMost relevant is selected, so some comments may have been filtered out.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":3722.944291999738,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}